-- Refs #337
-- Monk class trainers: 17 of the 19 (trainer_class 10) have gossip_menu_id 0, so talking to them opens no menu at all.
--
-- #337 as filed ("every class-10 trainer has zero npc_trainer rows") is NOT a bug: since patch 5.0.4 class abilities are
-- learned automatically on reaching the level (Wowpedia "Trainer", Patch changes: "Class abilities are now learnt
-- automatically by characters upon reaching the required level, without visiting trainers. Class trainers can now
-- separately reset characters' specialization, talents and glyphs."); the fork does it in Player::LearnSkillRewardedSpells
-- (Player.cpp:25760, GetLevel() < SpellLevel gate) and LearnSpecializationSpells (Player.cpp:25648). MoP 5.4.8 has the
-- same data (all trainer_class 10 NPCs npcflag 1/3, no trainer flag 16, no npc_trainer rows), and so does every other
-- class in LoA (only trainer_class 3 and 6 carry flag 16).
--
-- What IS missing: the "class trainer" menu. 9 of the 11 classes have a gossip menu on ~85-95% of their trainers with the
-- 5.0.4 options (OptionType 16-20: reset Class Specialization / Talents / Glyphs, Dual Specialization, Proving Grounds).
-- Monk has it on 2 of 19 (Aysa Cloudsinger 62419 menu 10373, Ji Firepaw 62445 menu 14248; same in MoP 5.4.8). The other 17
-- are the capital-city Monk trainers (Brewmaster Tzu, Ao Jian, Liu, Lanfen, Tseh Rah, Sho the Wise, Pan, Xi, Bao, Ting,
-- Lo, Gato, Zabrax, Shoyu, Laoxi, Pao, Mojo Stormstout).
--
-- Fix: give them Ji Firepaw's menu 14248 (same five 5.0.4 options; text 19888 "I have nothing to teach you, $c.", which is
-- the intended 5.0.4 behaviour of a trainer). Retail uses a per-NPC menu id whose text is not in either DB, so one shared
-- menu is used (menu rows are shared by many creatures elsewhere, e.g. 7263 by 7 warriors). Only rows still at 0 change.
--
-- VERIFY: SELECT entry, gossip_menu_id FROM creature_template WHERE trainer_class = 10;   -- all 14248 / 10373 / 14248
--   live: headless gossip-hello on Sho the Wise (62463, Eversong) lists "How do I reset my Class Specialization?" ...
-- ROLLBACK: UPDATE `creature_template` SET `gossip_menu_id` = 0 WHERE `entry` IN (62321, 62393, 62425, 62450, 62462, 62463, 62464, 63238, 63258, 63272, 63285, 63296, 63310, 63327, 63331, 63332, 63335);

UPDATE `creature_template` SET `gossip_menu_id` = 14248
WHERE `trainer_class` = 10 AND `gossip_menu_id` = 0
  AND `entry` IN (62321, 62393, 62425, 62450, 62462, 62463, 62464, 63238, 63258, 63272, 63285, 63296, 63310, 63327, 63331, 63332, 63335);
-- Refs #540 (closes the Westfall half; #485 was closed 2026-10-09)
-- Remove the temporary [J441] diagnostic binding that 2026_10_04_97_world_westfall_jangolode_trigger_diag.sql added:
-- the 8 "Livin' the Life" General Trigger spells (Shadowy Figure 79279/79283/79284/79287, Glubtok 79290/79292/79294/79297)
-- were bound to spell_westfall_jangolode_general_trigger, a logging-only SpellScript. The class is deleted from
-- src/server/scripts/EasternKingdoms/zone_westfall.cpp in the same build (together with the LogCredit hook on 79275), so
-- a leftover spell_script_names row would only make the loader report an unknown script name. The rows are the whole
-- of what _97 inserted; nothing else (the smart_scripts rewrite is _98, the 79275 binding is _75) is touched.
-- Rollback: re-run 2026_10_04_97_world_westfall_jangolode_trigger_diag.sql (it needs the C++ class back).

DELETE FROM `spell_script_names` WHERE `ScriptName` = 'spell_westfall_jangolode_general_trigger';
-- Refs #458
-- The Pride of Kezan (25066): "Shoot down 10 Gnomeregan Stealth Fighters" (Wowpedia The_Pride_of_Kezan, objective
-- "Gnomeregan Stealth Fighter shot down x10", read 2026-10-15). The fork's objective row asked for 1 kill: the release
-- DB carried the old "credit on accept" hack (SAI 38387 id0, removed by 2026_10_04_16), which only ever needed one
-- credit. MoP 5.4.8 (quest_objective questId 25066) has Amount 10 - the only Kezan/Lost Isles objective
-- row (116 quests, QuestSortID 4720/4737) that differs between the two DBs.
-- Rollback: UPDATE `quest_objective` SET `amount` = 1 WHERE `questId` = 25066 AND `objectId` = 39039 AND `type` = 0;

UPDATE `quest_objective` SET `amount` = 10 WHERE `questId` = 25066 AND `objectId` = 39039 AND `type` = 0;
-- Refs #440, #468, #471 (item 4). Quest 29798 "An Ancient Evil" (Wandering Isle, map 860, area 5833): one Vordraka.
--
-- Intended (Wowpedia "An Ancient Evil"): kill Vordraka, the Deep Sea Nightmare
-- (56009) with Aysa Cloudsinger's help. MoP 5.4.8 runs Jojo Ironbrow 55940 as SmartAI only (on accept: respawn the
-- static Vordraka) and has ONE static Vordraka (guid 563145, phaseMask 2) next to Aysa (563253, phaseMask 2).
--
-- Fork defect: 55940 also carries ScriptName npc_jojo_ironbrow (zone_wandering_island_south.cpp), whose
-- OnQuestAccept summons a SECOND, personal Vordraka at the same spot (TEMPSUMMON_TIMED_OR_DEAD_DESPAWN 10 min,
-- SetExplicitSeerGuid(player), phaseMask 12). Phases in area 5833 (spell_area, this fork's quest_end semantics =
-- "required status mask", SpellMgr.cpp:1061-1070):
--   29798 incomplete          -> 59073 (phase 2) only: the player sees the static Vordraka; the personal one (4|8)
--                                is invisible, never fights, never despawns early.
--   29798 complete / rewarded -> 59074 (phase 4): the static one is phased out and the still-alive personal Vordraka
--                                (phase 4|8, seer = the player) appears at the same spot, hostile, right after the kill.
-- So the duplicate is real, just not during the fight: a second Vordraka shows up after the quest objective is done.
-- Fix = MoP 5.4.8 design: drop the C++ binding, keep Jojo's SmartAI (55940 SAI row 0 already matches it) and the
-- shared static Vordraka (spawntimesecs 60). boss_vordraka (C++, Deep Sea Rupture fixed in 465a147b) stays on 56009;
-- its JustDied credits every player within 30 yd with 29798 incomplete, so a shared kill credits everyone.
-- The npc_jojo_ironbrow class stays registered in the core; ScriptMgr unloads unassigned scripts silently
-- (ScriptMgr::Initialize -> UnloadUnusedScripts), so no build is needed and no boot error is logged.
--
-- Test: t440 leg L7 (cansee 56009 before and after the kill, [SPELLWATCH] 117456/117287, objective 263987).
--
-- Rollback:
--   UPDATE `creature_template` SET `ScriptName` = 'npc_jojo_ironbrow' WHERE `entry` = 55940;
-- Re-runnable: plain UPDATE.

UPDATE `creature_template` SET `ScriptName` = '' WHERE `entry` = 55940;
-- Refs #182 (pool data inconsistencies, part 1 of 4: pool_template rows for the per-map pieces)
-- ERROR CLASS: `pool_gameobject`/`pool_creature` has spawns on multiple different maps ... skipped (PoolMgr.cpp:536,614) and
--   `pool_pool` has child pools on multiple maps (PoolMgr.cpp:709). A pool has ONE map (PoolTemplateData::MapId, set by the
--   first loaded member); every later member on another map is dropped, and because ObjectMgr only grid-spawns gameobjects/creatures
--   that are NOT in a pool (ObjectMgr.cpp:2132,2492), each dropped member NEVER spawns (a gathering-node / creature gap).
-- FIX (this file + _41, _42, _43): split every mixed-map pool into one pool per map. The original pool id keeps the map of its first
--   loaded member (the map the core already chose, so what works today is unchanged); each other map gets a NEW pool id
--   1000000 + old_id*8 + n (n = 1..3, ascending map id; the largest old id is 30184 so the range is far from existing ids)
--   with the same max_limit and the description "<old description> [map M, split of pool OLD]".
--   2335 pools are mixed-map (1738 members-only pools + 597 mother pools); 2534 new pieces. MoP 5.4.8 carries the same rows
--   (pool_template/pool_gameobject/pool_pool), i.e. it is inherited data, not an LoA regression.
-- This file only inserts the 2534 piece templates (INSERT IGNORE: re-runnable). _41/_42 move the members, _43 re-links mother pools.
-- Apply _40.._43 together: until the members are moved the new pools are empty ("Pool Id N is empty" lines).
-- VERIFY:  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pool_template WHERE entry >= 1000000;   -- 2534 after apply
-- UNDO:    DELETE FROM pool_template WHERE entry >= 1000000;  (after undoing _41/_42/_43)
-- Refs #182 (pool data inconsistencies, part 2 of 4: move mixed-map pool_gameobject members to the per-map pool)
-- ERROR CLASS: "`pool_gameobject` has gameobject spawns on multiple different maps for gameobject guid (G) in pool id (P), skipped."
--   3858 lines per boot (PoolMgr.cpp:614). Each skipped gameobject was never spawned (ObjectMgr.cpp:2492 skips pooled GOs).
-- ROWS: 1906 UPDATEs (one per pool+map), 3858 pool_gameobject rows moved from the old pool P to the new piece pool for the GO's own
--   map (gameobject.map). The rows that stay in P are those on the map of the pool's first loaded member (the core's current choice).
-- SOURCE OF TRUTH: gameobject.map of each guid (verified with the world DB; identical in the MoP 5.4.8 data). Needs _40 first.
-- Idempotent: each UPDATE is keyed on the exact guids AND the old pool_entry, so a second run matches 0 rows.
-- VERIFY:  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pool_gameobject pg JOIN gameobject g ON g.guid=pg.guid GROUP BY pg.pool_entry HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT g.map)>1; -- 0 rows (was 1736)
--          SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pool_gameobject WHERE pool_entry >= 1000000;  -- 3858
-- EXPECTED DBErrors.log DROP: 3858 lines ("multiple different maps for gameobject guid").
-- UNDO:    UPDATE pool_gameobject SET pool_entry = (FLOOR((pool_entry-1000000)/8)) WHERE pool_entry >= 1000000;  (old id = (new-1000000) div 8)
