-- Spawn models the core ignored: ObjectMgr::ChooseDisplayId only uses a creature row's `modelid` when that display is in the
-- creature's `creature_template_model` list (AC / TrinityCore rule), so 4746 spawns of 169 creatures showed a template model
-- instead - e.g. the Kezan Partygoers of the later Kezan phases (35202 35235 35236 35238) appeared as fire/visual stand-in
-- models 19725 / 21342 after 'Life of the Party'. Adds every missing (creature, spawn model) pair with Probability 0: the spawn
-- shows its own model, and the random choice for summons and model-less spawns is unchanged. Idempotent.
-- #938: 'Vault Cracking Toolset' (67476, The Great Bank Heist 14122) puts a dummy aura on the rider next to the vault's
-- control-vehicle aura. Only the control-vehicle half was unsaveable (Aura::CanBeSaved), so a player who logged out or disconnected
-- inside the vault kept the dummy aura for good, and the vault spell (67555) then failed with TARGET_AURASTATE: quest blocked.
